{
    "text": " Authentication and authorization are two ways of handling the user account on a website. Without authentication and authorization, user will not be able to access the website and its resources. Now if we difference between both of them, authentication is basically means to authenticate a user. Means to check if user is a client or user is a user of an application or not. If a user is not the application of a user, then it will not be able to have any account. And on the other hand, authorization is the way of checking the authority of an authenticated user. It means an user has the authority to use the specific area or use the specific features of a website. It is basically used in an admin or candidate based website where admin and candidates are using the same website but admin have some other access and user or candidate had some other access. This is basically used in role based authentication, control or role based authorization where we assign a role to a specific user and based on that role, we give features to the user, we give access to the user. Thanks.",
